> September 26, 2029 at 5:00 PM | WHAT NEEDS YOU | An Offer For Casey Marlow | Thomas Ashgrove passed on an offer. The production’s casting office offers you Casey Marlow in Abbott Elementary, a network television comedy on ABC, in a part the game made up. It pays $1,542.20 a day for two days, above the SAG-AFTRA Day Performer minimum of $1,402.00. Each shoot day runs eleven hours with an hour for lunch, so its last two hours of work are overtime at time and one-half, $578.33 more a day. A half-hour network comedy shot like a film, one camera, with room for alternate lines in the later takes. The work is from October 15, 2029 to October 16, 2029, in Los Angeles. The offer stands until September 29, 2029 at 5:00 PM. Casey Marlow is the game’s own character, in a season of Abbott Elementary the game imagines. It isn’t a real casting notice, and no one at the real production is casting it. The game sets this part’s shoot in Los Angeles: no page it read says where Abbott Elementary films. This work is in Los Angeles. You’d be away from October 12, 2029 to October 17, 2029. Warner Bros. Television and 20th Television book and pay for your flights, the cars and the hotel, as the game assumes for a part cast from New York. | Accept The Offer, Decline The Offer
