> April 15, 2030 at 9:00 AM | WHAT NEEDS YOU | An Offer For Inez | Thomas Ashgrove passed on an offer. Hargrove Casting offers you Inez in The Carnival On Prospect Street, a fictional serialized television drama without an audition. Hargrove Casting cast you as Rowan Kincaid in Lowell Falls Errand, where your work was Strong. It pays $1,542.20 a day for two days, above the SAG-AFTRA Day Performer minimum of $1,402.00. Each shoot day runs eleven hours with an hour for lunch, so its last two hours of work are overtime at time and one-half, $578.33 more a day. A drama whose story runs across the season, shot two episodes at a time: a day can hold scenes from both, so you play the middle of the story before its beginning, and the pages change more often. The work is from May 20, 2030 to May 21, 2030, in Los Angeles. The offer stands until April 18, 2030 at 5:00 PM. This work is in Los Angeles. You’d be away from May 17, 2030 to May 22, 2030. The production books and pays for your flights, the cars and the hotel, as the game assumes for a part away from where you live. | Accept The Offer, Decline The Offer
